SYNTHETIC ONLY
# This directory holds the labelled counterexample corpus (I-04) for
# the deterministic gate. The pattern is borrowed from
# inbox-job-tracker's tests/fixtures/emails.json -- a JSON array of
# {id, rule, expect, why, body, title, ...} records, each one a
# synthetic posting the gate should evaluate to `expect`.
#
# Every record's `why` field names the failure category. The
# `rule` field maps to a key in jobsearch/rule_why.WHY. The
# `expect` field is one of four verdict bands (snake_case,
# matching the gate's constants in jobsearch.rules):
#
#   strong_match       -- all rules satisfied, perfect fit
#   potential_match    -- all hard rules satisfied, soft signals differ
#   needs_research     -- a hard rule is uncertain; not enough data
#   not_suitable       -- a hard rule fails; the gate rejects
#
# The corpus is versioned by directory: v1, v2, ... A new version
# is a new directory, not an in-place edit. v1 is the shipped set
# (currently 21 fixtures); vN+1 is what a future contributor
# would create to add coverage.
#
# No real posting, real employer, real recruiter, or real candidate
# has ever been included here. Every record is synthetic, by
# construction, by this marker.
